<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Date Masamune</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1567–<a href="/years/1636">1636</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Date Masamune was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daimyo">daimyo</a> of north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, known as the 'one-eyed dragon'. He expanded the Date lands in Mutsu but submitted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a> in 1590 and later sided with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-ieyasu">Tokugawa Ieyasu</a>. He founded the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sendai">Sendai</a> and its domain, one of the largest in Tokugawa Japan, and sent an embassy to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in 1613.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/date-masamune.jpg" alt="Date Masamune" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kanō Yasunobu · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_DATE_Masamune.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
